US-028 is not complete, so I have not emitted the completion signal. The Vulkan backend is implemented, but one acceptance criterion needs hardware this WSL host doesn't have.

**Blocked:** "The same clear/readback fixture passes on Windows and native Linux with validation layers." I re-ran `engine_tests --suite gpu --backend vulkan` with the validation layer path set. It exits 3 `unsupported`: no hardware Vulkan 1.2 adapter with timeline semaphores. `/dev/dri` is absent, and the software ICD (lavapipe 21.2) lacks timeline semaphores. The PRD says software rendering and WSL don't replace the native Linux GPU report, so the story stays `passes: false`.

**Not changed this pass:** No engine, test, or doc source changed since the previous verified iteration, so I did not re-run the Windows or Linux quality gates. The last recorded run (in `.ralph-tui/progress.md`) had them passing: Windows `ValidateVendor`, `win-dev`, `win-debug`, and `win-unit` (21/21); the Windows GPU suite on RTX 5080 for DX12 and Vulkan with validation on; Linux `linux-dev`, `linux-debug`, and `linux-unit`; Linux GCC; and Linux ASan/UBSan.

**Still open:**
- The native Linux GPU clear/readback report, which needs a machine with a real Vulkan 1.2 hardware adapter.
- Surface-loss recovery is implemented but not exercised on either OS.
- GitHub CI has not been checked.
- `engine_bench` has no harness yet.

I appended a short entry to `.ralph-tui/progress.md` recording this pass. Once the native Linux report exists, `passes` can be set to true.
